# GoDaddy's "Go Daddy Secure Certificate Authority - G2" intermediate, used ONLY as an extra trust
# anchor for www.cysec.gov.cy (stocks/lib/watch.mjs EXTRA_CA_HOSTS, stocks/watch-sources.mjs).
#
# Why it is here: CySEC's server sends the wrong intermediate ("GoDaddy TLS Intermediate CA DV -
# R1v1") while its leaf certificate is issued by this one (leaf Authority Key Identifier
# 40:C2:BD:27:8E:CC:34:83:30:A2:33:D7:FB:6C:B3:F0:B4:2C:80:CE = this certificate's Subject Key
# Identifier). Browsers fetch the missing intermediate themselves; Node does not, and fails with
# UNABLE_TO_VERIFY_LEAF_SIGNATURE, so the announcements page was recorded as blocked (next-steps.md
# item 8). The certificate is public: https://certs.godaddy.com/repository/gdig2.crt (DER),
# converted with `openssl x509 -inform DER -outform PEM`, downloaded 2026-09-24. It is signed by
# "Go Daddy Root Certificate Authority - G2", already a trusted root, so trusting it adds no issuer
# the default store does not already chain to. The TLS check is never switched off.
#
# SHA-256 fingerprint 97:3A:41:27:6F:FD:01:E0:27:A2:AA:D4:9E:34:C3:78:46:D3:E9:76:FF:6A:62:0B:67:12:E3:38:32:04:1A:A6
